# Vulnerability details

## Impact

BathBuddy is a Vesting Wallet that payout withdrawers any bonus token they may have accrued while staking in the BathToken (cToken) 

This vesting occurs linearly over Unix time.

An attacker could steal almost all the bonusTokens in the BathBuddy Vesting Wallet.

## Proof of Concept

The root cause of this issue is that the amount of bonus token that a user is entitled to is based on their relative share of the pool’s total vested bonus token at the point of the withdraw call. It is calculated based on the user’s “spot” share in the pool.

Thus, it is possible for an attacker to deposit large amount of tokens into a BathToken Pool to gain significant share of the pool (e.g. 95%), and then withdraw the all the shares immediately.

Or even frontrun `bathHouse.claimRewards()` function call and increase his shares before it

