# Vulnerability details

## Impact

The BathBuddy staking contract is a modified version of the Synthetix staking contract. Here, the user's Bath Token balance is used to calculate rewards. However, the contract doesn't update its staking parameters correctly. The Synthetix contract uses the updateReward modifier to update staking parameters whenever a stake, unstake, or claim event happens. In the BathBuddy contract, since there are no direct staking or unstaking events, the updateReward function doesn't update staking attributes correctly. It only updates when the getReward function is called and not when someone mints BathToken (cToken) or redeems BathToken (cToken).

A hacker can exploit the system by minting, claiming, and redeeming Bath tokens without waiting for any period of time.

Here is the updateReward function/modifier which needs to called when user's bath Token balance changes but this contract fails to do so. 

```solidity
