# Vulnerability details

## Description
Added in the new version of `RubiconMarket` was the ability to create offers providing `owner` and `recipient`. Which will be the receivers of fees and sales of the offers.

There is however no check that these are not `address(0)`. Since most tokens revert on transfers to `address(0)` a user can create malicious small offers that will revert when they are filled.

This will brick a lot of functions like matching of orders and buy/sellAll. These orders can be created just above `_dust` to minimize funds needed.

## Impact
A user can cause reverts in market functions bricking the market.

## Proof of Concept
PoC test in `Market.t.sol`:
