# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Compound V2 has no protection against the first depositor breaking the internal exchange rate. This is a well known bug with vault-like contracts. The exchange rate between the underlying token to cToken depends on the cToken contract's balance of the underlying token. By inflating that balance through a direct transfer of tokens, the exchange rate can be manipulated so that the next time someone tries to mint cTokens, they receive none.

Here's a well written PoC by [akshaysrivastav](https://github.com/akshaysrivastav/first-deposit-bug-compv2)

