## Impact

Attacker is able to steal all reward tokens from the `BathBuddy` contract. This is possible because `userRewardsPerTokenPaid` is updated after the `tokenRewards` is set for a user. This means that `userRewardsPerTokenPaid` will always be 0 the first time there is a call to `updateReward(..)`. Therefore, an attacker can transfer the same bath tokens between multiple accounts they own and continuously call `getReward(..)` on the `BathHouseV2` contract. With this, they can drain all rewards tokens from the contract.

