# Vulnerability details

## Impact
_calculateDebt() implements a wrong calculation of interest for a debt and return wrong value, this can affect any function uses _calculateDebt to calculate the total debt. Make the borrowers get less or more interest than the actual one.

## Proof of Concept

    function _calculateDebt(
        address _bathToken,
        uint256 _startBlock,
        uint256 _borrowedAmount
    ) internal view returns (uint256 _debt) {
        uint256 _blockDelta = block.number - _startBlock;

        uint256 _interest = (
            (_borrowedAmount).mul(borrowRate(_bathToken).mul(_blockDelta))
        ).div(10 ** 18);
        _debt = _borrowedAmount.add(_interest);
    }

The calculation simply calculate the block delta and multiply it with the current borrow rate for bathToken. However, in CToken design the interest rate can change any time, so during the borrow time the rate may changed a lot of time, and it's inaccurate to use the latest rate then multiply it with the whole block delta. If the current rate is more than when the borrowers borrow, a borrower may get a much larger interest to pay than the actual.

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Implement the wrong calculation similar to the interestPerToken model used in CToken.

