# Vulnerability details

## Impact

In the Position contract, there is a critical vulnerability in the _borrowLimit function that may lead to unexpected behavior and a potential attack vector. The vulnerability stems from an unchecked underflow in the calculation of the _borrowDelta variable. This issue occurs when the _desiredAmount is less than the difference between _assetAmount and _loopBorrowed.

Affected Code:
```

function _borrowLimit(
    address _bathToken,
    address _asset,
    uint256 _assetAmount,
    uint256 _leverage
) internal returns (uint256 _limit, uint256 _lastBorrow) {
    ...
    if (_assetAmount > _desiredAmount) {
        uint256 _borrowDelta = _desiredAmount.sub(
            _assetAmount.sub(_loopBorrowed)
        );
        _lastBorrow = _borrowDelta.mul(WAD).div(_loopBorrowed);
        _limit++;
        break;
    }
    ...
}

```

The _borrowLimit function calculates the _limit and _lastBorrow based on the collateral, leverage, and other factors. The problematic code is within the if (_assetAmount > _desiredAmount) condition, where the _borrowDelta variable is calculated by subtracting _assetAmount.sub(_loopBorrowed) from _desiredAmount. Since there is no check to ensure that _desiredAmount is greater than or equal to _assetAmount.sub(_loopBorrowed), this subtraction can result in an underflow.

Attack Vector:

An attacker can exploit this vulnerability by crafting a malicious input that results in an underflow of the _borrowDelta calculation. This can lead to an incorrect calculation of _lastBorrow and _limit, which can further affect other parts of the contract such as the openPosition function.

If the _limit and _lastBorrow values are manipulated, this can result in undesired borrowing loops and potentially incorrect margin calculations, leading to losses for the contract owner and other users.


