# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Due to a missing state change of the variable `_head`, the function `_hide()` will always return false, therefore causing `cancel()` to fail as it requires `hide()` to return true for unsorted offers to be cancelled.

I consider the impact of this finding to be high as users will be unable to withdraw unsorted offers via the cancel function. Essentially, funds will be partially locked as they can still be bought, but cannot be cancelled. Which is not the intended purpose of the protocol. 

