# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The duration of the reward pool is set by the admin/owner calling setRewardsDuration(...) in BathBuddy.

However, there is no check to award investors based on the time they have invested.

So a legitimate user can invest right at the start, i.e. right after money is deposited into the pool and notifyRewardAmount(..) is called.

However, an attacker can come in at duration-1, invest a higher amount, and then immediately take out a significantly large amount in the very next transaction. 

For example if duration is 365 days, and the award pool has 10_000 in it, an attacker can come in a few seconds before the duration is up and take almost all of the award even though the legitimate user has been waiting for 365 days.

