# Vulnerability details

## Description

The `RubiconMarket` contract allows for users to interact with the protocol by making offers and trading ERC20 tokens. Users may place a trade and have the option of cancelling orders should they wish to take their tokens back however, users may lose tokens as the `cancel()` function may fail. 

This is due to the `isOfferSorted()` function assuming that one element in the orderbook is “unsorted” when this should already be considered as “sorted”. In addition to this, the `_unsort()` function does not consider a single element in the array where `_span[pay_gem][buy_gem] == 0`.

## Impact

A user may lose funds due to an undesirable or accidental trade and not being able to choose to cancel the offer because of a revert. In addition to this if an order is never matched, those tokens may be list.

## Proof of Concept

The proof of concept below outlines this scenario:

```solidity
function testCancelOrder() public {
  // Setup scenario - add to foundry tests

  TEST.mint(address(alice), 12 ether);
  TUSDC.mint(address(alice), 25 *1e6);

