# Vulnerability details

## Impact
A user can drain all rewards from the BathBuddy contract by transferring an amount of BathTokens between accounts and calling the `getReward()` function for each account. This will result in the BathBuddy contract administering rewards multiple times for the same holding.

## Proof of Concept
When a user has pending BathBuddy rewards they can call the `getReward` function on the `BathHouseV2` contract.

```solidity
function getReward(address buddy, address rewardsToken) external {
    IBathBuddy(buddy).getReward(IERC20(rewardsToken), msg.sender);
}
```

This calls the `getReward` function in the `BathBuddy` contract, passing along the `msg.sender` address.

The `getReward` function in the `BathBuddy` calls a `updateReward` modifier that updates accounting ahead of paying out the reward later in the execution.

```solidity
function getReward(
    IERC20 rewardsToken,
    address holderRecipient
)
    external
    override
    nonReentrant
    whenNotPaused
    updateReward(holderRecipient, address(rewardsToken))
    onlyBathHouse
{
    uint256 reward = tokenRewards[address(rewardsToken)][holderRecipient];
    if (reward > 0) {
        tokenRewards[address(rewardsToken)][holderRecipient] = 0;
        rewardsToken.safeTransfer(holderRecipient, reward);
        emit RewardPaid(holderRecipient, reward);
    }
}
```

