# Vulnerability details

## Impact
The V2Migrator contract is vulnerable to a reentrancy attack in the migrate function. The migrate function does not implement any reentrancy protection. This means that an attacker can repeatedly call the migrate function before the previous execution completes, leading to a double withdrawal from the bathTokenV1.

Furthermore, the migrate function uses a pattern of withdraw-then-transfer. This pattern is susceptible to reentrancy attacks because it is possible for an attacker to call a function on a malicious contract during the execution of the migrate function, before the transfer function is called, which can result in the attacker executing the migrate function again before the previous execution completes.

If this vulnerability is exploited, an attacker could drain the bathTokenV1 contract of all its funds, causing direct loss of funds to the users who hold tokens in the contract. Additionally, the attacker could potentially freeze the bathTokenV1 contract, making it impossible for legitimate users to withdraw their funds.


## Proof of Concept

```
